# Line endings, for the files where a carriage return is not cosmetic.
#
# The repository has deliberately had no .gitattributes: core.autocrlf handles C# fine, and the
# working tree being CRLF on Windows is what everyone here expects. These four patterns are the
# exceptions, and each is a build failure rather than a preference:
#
#   *.sh      a CR is part of the command, so bash reports `: command not found`
#   *.swift   swiftc accepts it, but the bundle script that drives swiftc does not
#   *.plist   plutil and codesign read these; CRLF in a plist is a parse risk for no gain
#   workflows the YAML holds bash `run:` blocks, so a CR reaches the shell the same way
#
# Marked eol=lf rather than -text: they are text and should still diff as text, they just must
# arrive as LF on every platform, including a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.swift text eol=lf
*.plist text eol=lf
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
